{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":1220,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.95,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"DP counting of binary strings avoiding 000 and 111\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 14 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". This is counting binary strings with no run of 3 same bits. Equivalent to sequences with max run length 2. Count via recurrence. Let a_n be number of strings length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit? Let's use DP with states: last bit and run length. States: (bit, runlen) where runlen=1 or 2. For n=1: two states: 0 runlen1, 1 runlen1. For each step, extend: if add same bit, runlen increases if <=2 else forbidden. So from runlen1 can go to runlen2 same bit. From runlen2 cannot add same bit. So transitions: from (b,1) -> (b,2) and (1-b,1). From (b,2) -> (1-b,1). Count.\n\nLet A_n = number of strings length n ending with runlen1. B_n = number ending with runlen2. Then recurrence: A_{n+1} = A_n + B_n (since from any state can add opposite bit to get runlen1). B_{n+1} = A_n (since only from runlen1 same bit). Base n=1: A_1=2 (both bits), B_1=0. Compute up to n=14.\n\nLet's iterate.\n\nn=1: A=2 B=0\nn=2: A= A1+B1 =2+0=2; B= A1=2 => A=2 B=2\nn=3: A= A2+B2 =2+2=4; B= A2=2 => A=4 B=2\nn=4: A=4+2=6; B=4 => A=6 B=4\nn=5: A=6+4=10; B=6 => A=10 B=6\nn=6: A=10+6=16; B=10 => A=16 B=10\nn=7: A=16+10=26; B=16 => A=26 B=16\nn=8: A=26+16=42; B=26 => A=42 B=26\nn=9: A=42+26=68; B=42 => A=68 B=42\nn=10: A=68+42=110; B=68 => A=110 B=68\nn=11: A=110+68=178; B=110 => A=178 B=110\nn=12: A=178+110=288; B=178 => A=288 B=178\nn=13: A=288+178=466; B=288 => A=466 B=288\nn=14: A=466+288=754; B=466 => A=754 B=466\n\nTotal strings length 14 = A+B = 754+466 = 1220.\n\nThus answer 1220. Provide final JSON."}}],"created":1790979902,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outp